  "answer": "The Bhagavad Gita guides decision-making in morally complex situations by advising individuals to consider the concept of oneness and the Law of Karma . It suggests that when we realize all of life is one, we stop hurting ourselves by hurting others, and what we do to others will one day be done to us. This principle, also known as \"Do unto others as you would have others do unto you,\" promotes treating others with love, compassion, and kindness . Additionally, the Tripura Rahasya considers the Bhagavad Gita as a valuable resource for emancipation and recommends reading it every day with love and care .",
